WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.580
Okay.

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:08.470
There is sort of an impeachment hearing against
Donald Trump that has started and I really

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.030
thought long and hard about how to approach
this story.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:18.170
Um, and the first sort of question we have
to ask is, is this really an impeachment hearing

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.140
that has started when the House Judiciary
Committee?

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:28.250
And uh, my sense is that it's not a, this
is being called a quote impeachment hearing,

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.670
but I don't actually think that that is the
right name for it.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:37.820
This is a hearing which depending on what
happens in some abstract sense could lead

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.380
to an actual impeachment inquiry.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.720
And this is already, if you're saying, David,
that sounds muddled.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.490
This is why I think that this is extraordinarily
problematic.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.490
Problematic.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:51.930
I try to tell you things as I see them truly
without over or understating the importance

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.160
of something.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.250
And the way that this has gone down so far
is seeming to me like a self destructive waste

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.250
of time.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.250
And I'll explain why.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.080
So yesterday the House Judiciary Committee
had a hearing.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:09.350
They started interviewing, uh, Donald Trump's
former campaign manager, Corey Lewandowski.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.400
Corey Lewandowski gave Democrats nothing.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.440
And in fact, he generated some really good
soundbites that right wing media and Donald

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.700
Trump are absolutely gushing about.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.060
He stonewalled.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:26.560
He brought a letter with him from the White
House, a lawyer, pat chip Alini saying that

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.770
executive privilege has been invoked.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.690
Now there is an obvious question about, wait
a second.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.560
Corey Lewandowski was the campaign manager,
meaning Donald Trump was not president at

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.170
the time that he was instructing Corey Lewandowski
to do things.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:44.380
Could executive privilege really even be asserted
given that Trump wasn't president at the time?

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.690
It's a question that would have to be fought
out legally and we don't have an answer to

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.690
that.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:53.890
In the immediate, um, uh, he refused to answer
questions about conversations with Donald

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:59.200
Trump, uh, like a very well behaved tool of
Donald Trump and Trump praising him for it.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.820
And in the end, this to me was a pointless
waste of time gong show this was going to

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.840
be the way it went down from day one.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.780
Lewandowski, even before the executive privilege
letter was written and presented, said that

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.790
he was looking forward to defending Donald
Trump in these hearings.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.860
They were never going to get anything from
Lewandowski.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:24.340
So then the question became in not getting
anything from Lewandowski can democrats make

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.340
him.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:32.520
And by Extension Donald Trump look bad enough,
look guilty enough to um, further the arguments

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.010
of, uh, impeachment and a real bonafide impeachment
inquiry.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.590
And I've said before, the whole point of an
impeachment inquiry if one were to be done,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.870
would not really be to remove Donald Trump
via impeachment because it's not going to

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:48.870
happen.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.050
A Republican Senate is not going to convict
Donald Trump on the basis of what's happened

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.930
so far, certainly not before the November
of 2020 election.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:59.290
The whole point in my view of an impeachment
inquiry would be to publicize the content

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:00.319
of the Mueller report.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:02.890
What's in the Mueller report is devastating
to Trump.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.270
Most of the public has not read the Mueller
report.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:09.920
So you do the impeachment inquiry to get the
content of the Mueller report out there front

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.920
and center.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.120
It distracts from Trump's campaigning.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.550
It may send Trump into a frenzy on Twitter
where he may end up further self incriminating.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:24.490
The only interesting thing that came out of
this hearing that could be advantageous to

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:30.580
democrats is that Corey Lewandowski refused
to say whether Donald Trump preemptively offered

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.920
him a pardon.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.250
It's very interesting.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.150
Ultimately, I don't think that's going to
go anywhere.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.950
We already know colloquially informally that
Donald Trump has in place implicitly dangled

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.560
pardons in front of people and it has had
absolutely no consequences.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.900
So I think that this ultimately is a mistake.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:53.349
I believe that if you are really going to
do a proper impeachment inquiry, you do it.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:58.110
You very clearly label it as such and it is
an impeachment investigation.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:03.320
This is a sort of, we've got some Democrats
saying they believe Trump is impeachable,

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:08.150
but this is just a hearing to talk to people,
which depending on what they say could become

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.730
a full blown impeachment inquiry or attempt
to impeach.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.540
I've said before, I'm fine with an impeachment
inquiry.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:19.499
If we're going to do it, I'm fine with saying
we're not going to do the impeachment inquiry.

00:04:19.499 --> 00:04:23.330
Let's just focus on removing Donald Trump
electorally in November of 2020 I'm fine with

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:30.509
it either way, but this off-handed hearing
of something that could sort of de facto be

00:04:30.509 --> 00:04:35.661
an investigation into whether there should
be impeachment vote the guy out in 2020 and

00:04:35.661 --> 00:04:36.661
remove him.

00:04:36.661 --> 00:04:40.789
And if you look at the media coverage over
the last 24 hours of this right wing media

00:04:40.789 --> 00:04:42.520
is doing what we know they were going to do.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.770
They are going to say, this is a partisan
witch hunt.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.219
Corey Lewandowski went in there, he gave them
nothing.

00:04:48.219 --> 00:04:49.550
Trump's happening it.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:50.550
Trump's happy with it.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.449
It unites the right around.

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:55.719
We're not going to let Democrats pull this
off.

00:04:55.719 --> 00:05:00.449
And then on the left you hear Democrats saying
Lewandowski stonewalling.

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:04.819
He's not answering questions, et Cetera, but
this is what they've been doing all along.

00:05:04.819 --> 00:05:07.870
There is no additional benefit to this.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:14.759
So it, it's, I'm calling this a halfhearted
pseudo impeachment, maybe hearing where witnesses

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:15.770
will say nothing.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.879
I don't know what type of PR they expect to
get.

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:22.289
That's beneficial to the cause of removing
Donald Trump, but it is seeming to me very

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:23.289
miscalculated.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.250
Now I'm willing to have my mind changed.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:30.460
If you saw this and you thought, yeah, this
is good, this is going to help us achieve

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.229
something and let me know what that is and
how it's going to help achieve it.

00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:39.550
As you know, I, I just call things what they
are and this is the way this looks to me.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:40.770
Let me know what you think.

